<title>HUNGARY: Hungary three-month bill yield drops to 20.54 pct.</title>
<headline>Hungary three-month bill yield drops to 20.54 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average annual yield on the latest issue of Hungary's three-month discount treasury bills was set by auction at 20.54 percent, down from 20.68 percent at an auction one week ago, the Government Debt Management Agency said on its Reuter page  HTBN.</p>
<p>    Total on offer	     5,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total bids received     10,097.39 million forints</p>
<p>    Total allocated	    5,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total issued		 5,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Average annual yield	    20.54 pct</p>
<p>    Average price		     95.1285 pct</p>
</text>
